Hi Dean,

That is a good suggestion as I had once a problem that the order was changing. So we will take that onboard and allow to have the order specified.

Currently the order is done via:

order(pop(x))

means it is ordered by the pop (and alphatically).

So the “trick” until we implement it,  is to relabel the pop factor, so that population order and alphabetical order are identical

You can do that via

#check the levels

levels(pop(pp))

levels(pop(pp)) <- c(…yournewlables in the order, that the alphabetical order matches the one you want to have in the genepop output)

Admittedly not really a good solution, but should work.

Cheers, Bernd

